## 4. Conclusions
In summary, SALE was carried out with TMU MOFs under ultrasound method. The porosity of daughter frameworks has been investigated by BET measurements using $\ensuremath{\mathbf{N}}_{2}$ at 77 K. We have shown that SALE can enhance the surface area and lead to higher $\mathsf{C O}_{2}$ sorption capacity. The $\ensuremath{\mathbf{N}}_{2}$ sorption of daughter frameworks is 3–20 times greater than that of as-synthesized parents MOFs. Among ligands, L6 has the lowest basicity of the azine group in the ligand. As a result, free L6 was finally able to exchange all the as-synthesized parents MOFs. This study confirmed that the construction method is an important factor in the adsorption performance.
